# EXAMPLE ontology.ttl for a GymAct consumer's own capability facts.
#
# Rename this file to `ontology.ttl` after editing. It declares ZERO new
# RDF vocabulary (no new rdfs:Class, no new owl:*Property) -- only
# `sosa:Procedure` INSTANCES (data, not vocabulary), matching GymAct's own
# `.claude/rules/ontology.md` rule ("Public Vocabularies First, No Custom
# TBox") and satisfying the real GymAct SHACL shape
# `urn:gymact:shape:capability` (fetched via `gymact export-profile`, see
# this pack's README -- never hand-invent your own shape).
#
# Each individual below corresponds to one capability your
# `EnvironmentProvider`/`Environment` implementation actually exposes to
# GymAct (see docs/integrations/ in the gymact repo for how a provider is
# registered via the `gymact.providers` entry-point group). Do not declare
# a capability here that your provider does not really implement --
# per GymAct's consequence law, `request accepted != world changed !=
# objective verified`, and this ontology.ttl is a real, checkable claim
# about what your provider does, not aspirational documentation.

@prefix dct: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .
@prefix sosa: <http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/> .

# Replace `example-system` below with your own system's slug throughout
# this file (e.g. `autofde-lab`), and replace the two example capabilities
# with your provider's real ones. `dct:title` becomes the generated
# operation `id` (and, prefixed with your MCP tool namespace, the
# generated MCP tool name); `dct:type` MUST be one of the two real GymAct
# consequence-class IRIs below -- any other value is refused by the real
# SHACL shape at sync time, before any file is generated.

<urn:example-system:capability:list-something>
    a sosa:Procedure ;
    dct:title "list-something" ;
    dct:type <urn:gymact:consequence:read> .

<urn:example-system:capability:do-something>
    a sosa:Procedure ;
    dct:title "do-something" ;
    dct:type <urn:gymact:consequence:do> .
